   "population": "loggers",
   "story": "The state hatchery on Silver Run raised rainbow and brook trout for every lake in the valley: a long raceway shed open above its pony walls, the hatch house with its incubator stacks, chiller and feed room, the manager's cottage and a little intake dam with a catwalk over the weir. When the Cordon came up the creek it took the hatchery as a water-testing post: Lieutenant Okonkwo, a contract hydrologist and three soldiers sampled the creek every four hours to learn whether the Bloom travelled in water. It did. The trout died first, then the raceways furred white. Gordon Haskell's crew kept feeding fish that were not there and coughing in their waders. The Cordon boarded the shed, nailed the lab door shut against it and locked its samples and its cache in the chiller; Private Sato kept climbing to the sampler on the intake catwalk, where nothing could follow him, until the day he didn't climb down. Gordon went up the creek to look for the source and never came back. June is still in the cottage.",
